Z||000000||mshill||12-21-1999||08:03 PM||||I found the following ad on e-bay to be quite interesting.  Why exactly would and 86 GT be classified as a 'CLASSIC' in 2001? <P>Ad Text:<P>1986 Fiero GT! V-6, very fast, very COOL! Jet black, sun roof, power windows, AM/FM cassette, tilt, cruise, PB, ONLY 90K ACTUAL MILES! This is<BR>     rapidly becoming a collector's item, in 2001 it will become a "CLASSIC" Well maintained and taken care of, still in SWEET shape! We paid $5,000.00 for it in<BR>     1996 (and it has only gone up in price & collectibility since then!) and we are starting it here at $3,999.99 with NO RESERVE! This is a STEAL for any<BR>     collector as the GT models (only the GT's, the rest just don't cut it!) of Fiero are becoming true collectibles! There is only 2 1/2 years worth of GT Fieros with<BR>     this one's body style ('86. '87, & a short run # of '88's), so, bid now as it will be sold to the highest bidder! <P>||||reg||4
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||12-21-1999||09:27 PM||||"so, bid now as it will be sold to the highest bidder!"<P>Really?? And to think all this time I thought it was the low bidder... silly me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||fiero56||12-21-1999||09:56 PM||||I don't know about all states, but here in Ohio, after a a car model reaches a certain age, it can be classified as a classic. Guy down the street from me has a '77 mustang, and he has "classic" plates.  I also saw "classic" plates on a few older model Fieros at the Columbus show. Plus, once your car reaches this status here in Ohio, e-check is no longer required <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. I'm not sure what the age is, probly somewhere around 20-25yrs old. Definitly not Fieros yet.<BR>This guy sounds a little out there. I think Monkey needs to offer the guy some medication. We'll give ya' another chance Monkeyman. Just as a show of how friendly Fiero folk are. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||12-21-1999||10:07 PM||||Looks like I arrived just in time.  In Indiana, we call them "antiques", not "classics", but it's probably the same thing.  After 20 years, we qualify for an Antiques plate and get some kind of small discount on the registration.  I wouldn't get one because the plates are ugly and I have a personalized plate coming in January.  (Of course it'll say, "MNKY MAN"!!)<P>If you'll also notice, he thinks that they produced the fastback in all of '86 and only part of '88.  I emailed him and set him straight.  I'm sure he'll send me some $$ in appreciation! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I also sent him the name of my "special" doctor. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
